 ### Boot, Shutdown, Erase, Delete
 
+> **Always ask the user before running `simctl erase`, `simctl delete`, or
+> `rm` on anything under `~/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator`.** They destroy
+> app data and devices that may belong to other projects, and can't be undone.
+> Name the exact command and devices affected, and wait for a yes every time.
+
 ```bash
 # Boot a specific device
 xcrun simctl boot <UDID>
